  "title": "Basics 1",
  "description": "Learn your very first Korean words and sentences! Meet people, name foods, and start talking about what you eat and drink.",
  "guidebook": "# Welcome to Basics 1! 🇰🇷\n\nKorean sentences often drop the subject because the verb ending tells you who's doing what. The verb **이다** (to be) is rarely used alone — instead, adjectives and descriptive verbs attach **-이에요/예요** for \"is/am/are.\"\n\n**Particles** are small markers after nouns:\n- **은/는** = topic marker (\"as for…\")\n- **이/가** = subject marker (\"…is the one\")\n\n**To eat** = **먹다** → **먹어요** (eats / I eat)\n**To drink** = **마시다** → **마셔요** (drinks / I drink)\n\n**Word order:** Subject + Object + Verb. Example: \"I eat bread\" → **저는 빵을 먹어요** (jeo-neun ppang-eul meo-geo-yo). The object marker **을/를** marks what is eaten or drunk.\n\n**Politeness:** **-요** endings are polite but friendly — perfect for beginners!",
